  "description": "health.v1 §5, \"is this service's clock ahead?\" (§2.5): what one subscriber heard of one service during its reading, in arrival order -> the answer. A case gives presence, descriptor and face as judgements.json writes them. heard: the deliveries, each \"status\" (a put of state/status, a change or a re-put: a confirmation), \"status_deleted\" (a delete of state/status, which is no confirmation), \"clock_ahead\" (a stream/faults sample whose code is clock_ahead, whatever its level and its stamp) or \"fault\" (a stream/faults sample with any other code). expect.answer is yes, no, unobservable or not_asked: yes on a clock_ahead fault with no confirmation heard after it; no when a confirmation was heard after the last clock_ahead fault, or with none heard; unobservable when neither was heard, since the faults' silence is their normal state; not_asked when the service is absent or its descriptor does not list health.v1, as the first question's. A fault heard answers whatever else presence says. expect.reason: clock_ahead, confirmed, nothing_heard, absent or not_listed."
